d", "sub_issues_summary": {"total": 0, "completed": 0, "percent_completed": 0}, "issue_dependencies_summary": {"blocked_by": 0, "total_blocked_by": 0, "blocking": 0, "total_blocking": 0}, "body": "`TimestampSigner` works with no problem in Python 3.6.6, but `Signer` gives the following error:\r\n\r\n```\r\n  File \"/path/to/python3.6/site-packages/itsdangerous.py\", line 353, in sign\r\n    return value + want_bytes(self.sep) + self.get_signature(value)\r\nTypeError: must be str, not bytes\r\n```", "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pallets/itsdangerous/issues/101/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "timeline_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pallets/itsdangerous/issues/101/timeline", "performed_via_github_app": null, "state_reason": "completed", "pinned_comment": null, "score": 1.0}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pallets/itsdangerous/issues/40", "repository_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pallets/itsdangerous", "labels_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pallets/itsdangerous/issues/40/labels{/name}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pallets/itsdangerous/issues/40/comments", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pallets/itsdangerous/issues/40/events", "html_url": "https://github.com/pallets/itsdangerous/issues/40", "id": 50037189, "node_id": "MDU6SXNzdWU1MDAzNzE4OQ==", "number": 40, "title": "add expiry date to TimestampSigner", "user": {"login": "fnep", "id": 2083099, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjIwODMwOTk=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2083099?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/fnep", "html_url": "https://github.com/fnep", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fnep/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fnep/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fnep/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fnep/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fnep/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fnep/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fnep/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fnep/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fnep/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "locked": true, "assignees": [], "milestone": null, "comments": 2, "created_at": "2014-11-25T15:01:09Z", "updated_at": "2021-02-09T02:49:05Z", "closed_at": "2016-04-12T20:11:04Z", "assignee": null, "author_association": "NONE", "issue_field_values": [], "type": null, "active_lock_reason": "resolved", "sub_issues_summary": {"total": 0, "completed": 0, "percent_completed": 0}, "issue_dependencies_summary": {"blocked_by": 0, "total_blocked_by": 0, "blocking": 0, "total_blocking": 0}, "body": "Could you please add some kind of expiry date to the TimestampSigner? I want to allow my users to decide how long their links should be valid. Currently i have to include the current timestamp (by using the TimestampSigner) and the max age the user wants. So in such a case it would be much more helpful to handle the integrated Timestamp as expiry date and not as creation date ... but even if i would handle the date check myself, it seems not to be possible to define the now-timestamp used by the TimestampSigner.\n", "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pallets/itsdangerous/issues/40/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "timeline_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pallets/itsdangerous/issues/40/timeline", "performed_via_github_app": null, "state_reason": "completed", "pinned_comment": null, "score": 1.0}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pallets/itsdangerous/issues/11", "repository_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pallets/itsdang